# L §4.6 step 1: "every key it states equals the corresponding key in k (a * matches every key; a range a..b
# matches every key from a to b in index order, on any index ...)"; step 3.2: "the row that states more keys (a
# specific row beats a default row) ... so [t1_15, *] (one) beats a keyless row (none), and [t5_023, 1..60] beats
# [t5_023, *]".  x[p1, 5] is the range row (2), x[p1, 70] the [p1, *] row (1), x[p2, 5] the keyless row (0).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

index ps = [p1, p2]
index ns = 1..80
input x[p in ps, n in ns]: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x = 0
  x[p1, *] = 1
  x[p1, 1..60] = 2

ask q1: x[p1, 5], x[p1, 70], x[p2, 5]
=== expect
q1: (2, 1, 0)
  cut 2026-12-31
